the aquamarine waters of the  mediterranean surrounded by craggy  cliffs keep luring tourists to these  coves  however vacationers aren't the reason  this small italian island has made  headlines in recent years  in 2013 368 migrants and refugees died  when an overcrowded boat capsized near  lampedusa it was one of the worst  shipwrecks in modern european history  francesco barrata's father was fishing  with a friend when he heard cries for  help he rescued a dozen people and  became a national hero  the people who think all migrants are  criminals don't understand what it means  to suffer for something  and forget that the westerners have  exploited the same africa they came from  after people protested the days when  asylum seekers arrived and roamed the  narrow streets are long gone  now their presence is invisible to most  prompting one woman to accuse our crew  of spreading misinformation  there is a problem when the sea is very  calm like today we see at least 1 500  people arriving each week they are  immediately transferred to cilicy or  somewhere else we don't see them on the  island  yet the migrant welcome center is  overflowing  the uptick in arrivals coincides with  the collapse of prime minister mario  draghi's coalition government this month  he announced his resignation twice  far-right and populist parties torpedoed  draghi's government and are expected to  prevail in snap elections on september  25th  the maguiri siblings come from one of  the oldest families on lampadusa they  make a living selling produce out of a  truck in the city center  we should vote for the far right and  give them an opportunity to run the  country before we say they are not good  currently migrants are coming here every  day without any rules  barrata hopes italians won't allow far  right and populist candidates to  scapegoat migrants  almost a decade later his father has  remained in contact with some of the  people he rescued and he says the  sadness in their eyes remains natasha  ghanim al jazeera lampadusa italy
 

